{"id":"mahabharata-6-041","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":41,"title":"एकचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 41 · Yudhishthira seeks the elders' blessing","summary":{"en":"After the Gita, Yudhishthira lays down his arms and walks to Bhishma, Drona, Kripa and Shalya to ask leave to fight. Each blesses him and promises victory, and Bhishma reveals that he cannot be defeated while he fights but will give counsel.","kn":"ಗೀತೆಯ ನಂತರ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಆಯುಧ ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಭೀಷ್ಮ, ದ್ರೋಣ, ಕೃಪ, ಶಲ್ಯರ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗಿ ಯುದ್ಧಕ್ಕೆ ಅನುಮತಿ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಆಶೀರ್ವದಿಸಿ ಜಯ ಹಾರೈಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ತಾನು ಹೋರಾಡುವವರೆಗೆ ಸೋಲಿಸಲಾಗದು, ಆದರೆ ಸಲಹೆ ನೀಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गीता के बाद युधिष्ठिर शस्त्र रखकर भीष्म, द्रोण, कृप और शल्य के पास जाकर युद्ध की अनुमति माँगते हैं। सब आशीर्वाद देकर विजय की कामना करते हैं, और भीष्म कहते हैं कि लड़ते हुए वे अजेय हैं पर सलाह देंगे।","te":"గీత తరువాత యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఆయుధాలు వదిలి భీష్ముడు, ద్రోణుడు, కృపుడు, శల్యుల వద్దకు వెళ్లి యుద్ధానికి అనుమతి కోరతాడు. అందరూ ఆశీర్వదించి జయం కోరతారు; భీష్ముడు తాను పోరాడుతున్నంతవరకు అజేయుడనని, కానీ సలహా ఇస్తానని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"கீதைக்குப் பின் யுதிஷ்டிரர் ஆயுதங்களை விட்டு பீஷ்மர், த்ரோணர், கிருபர், சல்யர் ஆகியோரிடம் சென்று போருக்கு அனுமதி கேட்கிறார். அனைவரும் ஆசிர்வதித்து வெற்றி வாழ்த்துகின்றனர்; பீஷ்மர் தாம் போரிடும்வரை வெல்ல முடியாதவர் ஆயினும் ஆலோசனை தருவதாகக் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ഗീതോപദേശത്തിനുശേഷം യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ആയുധം താഴെവെച്ച് ഭീഷ്മർ, ദ്രോണർ, കൃപർ, ശല്യർ എന്നിവരെ സമീപിച്ച് യുദ്ധത്തിന് അനുമതി ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ഓരോരുത്തരും അനുഗ്രഹിച്ച് ജയം വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുമ്പോൾ തന്നെ തോൽപ്പിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്നും എന്നാൽ ഉപദേശം നൽകാമെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.41; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो धनंजयं दृष्ट्वा बाणगाण्डीवधारिणम् ।\nपुनरेव महानादं व्यसृजन्त महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Arjuna with his bow Gandiva and arrows, the great chariot-warriors raised a mighty roar once more."}},{"n":2,"text":"पाण्डवाः सोमकाश्चैव ये चैषामनुयायिनः ।\nदध्मुश्च मुदिताः शङ्खान्वीराः सागरसंभवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, the Somakas and their followers, all delighted, blew their sea-born conch shells."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो भेर्यश्च पेश्यश्च क्रकचा गोविषाणिकाः ।\nसहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त ततः शब्दो महानभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then kettledrums, tabors, cymbals and cowhorns were suddenly all struck together, and a tremendous din arose."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ देवाः सगन्धर्वाः पितरश्च जनेश्वर ।\nसिद्धचारणसंघाश्च समीयुस्ते दिदृक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of men, gods with gandharvas, the ancestors, and hosts of siddhas and charanas gathered, wishing to watch."}},{"n":5,"text":"ऋषयश्च महाभागाः पुरस्कृत्य शतक्रतुम् ।\nसमीयुस्तत्र सहिता द्रष्टुं तद्वैशसं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sages too, with Indra, the hundred-sacrificer, at their head, assembled there to witness that vast slaughter."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो दृष्ट्वा युद्धाय सुसमुद्यते ।\nते सेने सागरप्रख्ये मुहुः प्रचलिते नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, seeing the two armies, vast as oceans, ready for battle and surging again and again, O king,"}},{"n":7,"text":"विमुच्य कवचं वीरो निक्षिप्य च वरायुधम् ।\nअवरुह्य रथात्तूर्णं पद्भ्यामेव कृताञ्जलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"took off his armor, laid down his excellent weapon, and quickly stepping down from his chariot went on foot with folded hands."}},{"n":8,"text":"पितामहमभिप्रेक्ष्य धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nवाग्यतः प्रययौ येन प्राङ्मुखो रिपुवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Silent, facing east, King Yudhishthira, the son of Dharma, walked toward the enemy host, looking toward his grandfather Bhishma."}},{"n":9,"text":"तं प्रयान्तमभिप्रेक्ष्य कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ।\nअवतीर्य रथात्तूर्णं भ्रातृभिः सहितोऽन्वयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him go, Arjuna, son of Kunti, quickly got down from his chariot and followed him with his brothers."}},{"n":10,"text":"वासुदेवश्च भगवान्पृष्ठतोऽनुजगाम ह ।\nयथामुख्याश्च राजानस्तमन्वाजग्मुरुत्सुकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed Vasudeva Krishna followed behind, and the foremost kings came after him, full of eagerness."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"किं ते व्यवसितं राजन्यदस्मानपहाय वै ।\nपद्भ्यामेव प्रयातोऽसि प्राङ्मुखो रिपुवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, what is your plan, that you leave us and walk on foot toward the enemy army, facing east?"}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"क्व गमिष्यसि राजेन्द्र निक्षिप्तकवचायुधः ।\nदंशितेष्वरिसैन्येषु भ्रातॄनुत्सृज्य पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where will you go, O king of kings, with your armor and weapons laid aside, abandoning your brothers while the enemy troops stand armored?"}},{"text":"नकुल उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nakula said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"एवंगते त्वयि ज्येष्ठे मम भ्रातरि भारत ।\nभीर्मे दुनोति हृदयं ब्रूहि गन्ता भवान्क्व नु ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you, my eldest brother, act like this, O Bharata, fear tortures my heart. Tell me where you are going."}},{"text":"सहदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अस्मिन्रणसमूहे वै वर्तमाने महाभये ।\nयोद्धव्ये क्व नु गन्तासि शत्रूनभिमुखो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"With this great fearful host in motion and a battle to be fought, where are you going, O king, toward the enemy?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमाभाष्यमाणोऽपि भ्रातृभिः कुरुनन्दन ।\nनोवाच वाग्यतः किंचिद्गच्छत्येव युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though his brothers spoke to him thus, O delight of the Kurus, Yudhishthira said nothing, and silently kept walking."}},{"n":16,"text":"तानुवाच महाप्राज्ञो वासुदेवो महामनाः ।\nअभिप्रायोऽस्य विज्ञातो मयेति प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wise and great-minded Vasudeva spoke to them, almost laughing: \"I understand his intention.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एष भीष्मं तथा द्रोणं गौतमं शल्यमेव च ।\nअनुमान्य गुरून्सर्वान्योत्स्यते पार्थिवोऽरिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This king will fight his enemies only after paying respects to all his elders: Bhishma, Drona, Gautama Kripa and Shalya.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"श्रूयते हि पुराकल्पे गुरूनननुमान्य यः ।\nयुध्यते स भवेद्व्यक्तमपध्यातो महत्तरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For it is heard from ancient times that a man who fights without honoring his elders is surely condemned by his superiors.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अनुमान्य यथाशास्त्रं यस्तु युध्येन्महत्तरैः ।\nध्रुवस्तस्य जयो युद्धे भवेदिति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But one who honors his superiors as the scriptures prescribe and then fights, his victory in battle is certain. That is my view.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति कृष्णे तु धार्तराष्ट्रचमूं प्रति ।\nहाहाकारो महानासीन्निःशब्दास्त्वपरेऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Krishna was speaking thus, a great cry of dismay arose in Dhritarashtra's army, and others fell silent."}},{"n":21,"text":"दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरं दूराद्धार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैनिकाः ।\nमिथः संकथयां चक्रुर्नेशोऽस्ति कुलपांसनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Yudhishthira from afar, Dhritarashtra's soldiers whispered to one another, \"This disgrace of the family is lost!\""}},{"n":22,"text":"व्यक्तं भीत इवाभ्येति राजासौ भीष्ममन्तिकात् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरः ससोदर्यः शरणार्थं प्रयाचकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Clearly this king Yudhishthira, with his brothers, is afraid and is coming to Bhishma to beg for protection.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"धनंजये कथं नाथे पाण्डवे च वृकोदरे ।\nनकुले सहदेवे च भीतोऽभ्येति च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How can the Pandava be afraid, when Arjuna is his protector, and Bhima, Nakula and Sahadeva too?\""}},{"n":24,"text":"न नूनं क्षत्रियकुले जातः संप्रथिते भुवि ।\nयथास्य हृदयं भीतमल्पसत्त्वस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely he was not born in a famous warrior family, for his heart is frightened in battle, like one of little spirit.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्ते क्षत्रियाः सर्वे प्रशंसन्ति स्म कौरवान् ।\nहृष्टाः सुमनसो भूत्वा चैलानि दुधुवुः पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all those warriors praised the Kauravas, and glad and cheerful, they waved their garments about."}},{"n":26,"text":"व्यनिन्दन्त ततः सर्वे योधास्तत्र विशां पते ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं ससोदर्यं सहितं केशवेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the soldiers there, O lord of the people, also reproached Yudhishthira, together with his brothers and Keshava."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततस्तत्कौरवं सैन्यं धिक्कृत्वा तु युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nनिःशब्दमभवत्तूर्णं पुनरेव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kaurava army, having cursed Yudhishthira, quickly fell silent again, O lord of the people."}},{"n":28,"text":"किं नु वक्ष्यति राजासौ किं भीष्मः प्रतिवक्ष्यति ।\nकिं भीमः समरश्लाघी किं नु कृष्णार्जुनाविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What will this king say? What will Bhishma reply? What will Bhima, so proud in battle, say, or Krishna and Arjuna?\""}},{"n":29,"text":"विवक्षितं किमस्येति संशयः सुमहानभूत् ।\nउभयोः सेनयो राजन्युधिष्ठिरकृते तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great doubt arose in both armies, O king, about what Yudhishthira meant to say."}},{"n":30,"text":"स विगाह्य चमूं शत्रोः शरशक्तिसमाकुलाम् ।\nभीष्ममेवाभ्ययात्तूर्णं भ्रातृभिः परिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He plunged into the enemy host, thick with arrows and spears, and, surrounded by his brothers, went straight to Bhishma."}},{"n":31,"text":"तमुवाच ततः पादौ कराभ्यां पीड्य पाण्डवः ।\nभीष्मं शांतनवं राजा युद्धाय समुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava king, clasping the feet of Bhishma, son of Shantanu, who stood ready for war, spoke to him."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"आमन्त्रये त्वां दुर्धर्ष योत्स्ये तात त्वया सह ।\nअनुजानीहि मां तात आशिषश्च प्रयोजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask your leave, invincible one. I shall fight you, grandfather. Give me your permission and bless me.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"यद्येवं नाभिगच्छेथा युधि मां पृथिवीपते ।\nशपेयं त्वां महाराज पराभावाय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you had not come to me like this before battle, O lord of the earth, I would have cursed you for your defeat, great king.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"प्रीतोऽस्मि पुत्र युध्यस्व जयमाप्नुहि पाण्डव ।\nयत्तेऽभिलषितं चान्यत्तदवाप्नुहि संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased, my son. Fight and win, Pandava, and may you gain in battle whatever else you desire.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"व्रियतां च वरः पार्थ किमस्मत्तोऽभिकाङ्क्षसि ।\nएवं गते महाराज न तवास्ति पराजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Choose a boon, Partha. What do you wish from me? Since you have come thus, O great king, you will not be defeated.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"अर्थस्य पुरुषो दासो दासस्त्वर्थो न कस्यचित् ।\nइति सत्यं महाराज बद्धोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man is the slave of wealth, but wealth is no one's slave. This is true, great king, and I am bound by wealth to the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"अतस्त्वां क्लीबवद्वाक्यं ब्रवीमि कुरुनन्दन ।\nहृतोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरव्य युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So I speak to you like a eunuch, delight of the Kurus: I am held by wealth. What do you want, other than my not fighting?\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"मन्त्रयस्व महाप्राज्ञ हितैषी मम नित्यशः ।\nयुध्यस्व कौरवस्यार्थे ममैष सततं वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Counsel me, wise one, always wishing me well, and fight for the Kaurava side. That is my constant boon.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"राजन्किमत्र साह्यं ते करोमि कुरुनन्दन ।\nकामं योत्स्ये परस्यार्थे ब्रूहि यत्ते विवक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What help can I give you in this, delight of the Kurus? I will fight on the other side as I please. Say what you wish to say.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"कथं जयेयं संग्रामे भवन्तमपराजितम् ।\nएतन्मे मन्त्रय हितं यदि श्रेयः प्रपश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How can I defeat you, who are unconquered, in battle? Tell me that, if you see it as good for me.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"न तं पश्यामि कौन्तेय यो मां युध्यन्तमाहवे ।\nविजयेत पुमान्कश्चिदपि साक्षाच्छतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son of Kunti, I see no man who could defeat me as I fight in battle, not even Indra himself.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"हन्त पृच्छामि तस्मात्त्वां पितामह नमोऽस्तु ते ।\nजयोपायं ब्रवीहि त्वमात्मनः समरे परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I ask you this, grandfather, and bow to you: tell me the means by which you may be defeated in battle by others.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"न शत्रुं तात पश्यामि समरे यो जयेत माम् ।\nन तावन्मृत्युकालो मे पुनरागमनं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear child, I see no enemy who could beat me in battle, and my time of death has not yet come. Come to me again.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो वाक्यं भीष्मस्य कुरुनन्दन ।\nशिरसा प्रतिजग्राह भूयस्तमभिवाद्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, delight of the Kurus, accepted Bhishma's word with bowed head, and bowing to him again,"}},{"n":45,"text":"प्रायात्पुनर्महाबाहुराचार्यस्य रथं प्रति ।\nपश्यतां सर्वसैन्यानां मध्येन भ्रातृभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"the mighty-armed king went with his brothers toward the chariot of the teacher Drona, through the middle of the whole watching army."}},{"n":46,"text":"स द्रोणमभिवाद्याथ कृत्वा चैव प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nउवाच वाचा दुर्धर्षमात्मनिःश्रेयसं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having greeted Drona and circled him respectfully, he spoke to the invincible one words for his own highest good."}},{"n":47,"text":"आमन्त्रये त्वां भगवन्योत्स्ये विगतकल्मषः ।\nजयेयं च रिपून्सर्वाननुज्ञातस्त्वया द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask your leave, revered one. I shall fight free of sin, and with your permission may I defeat all my enemies, O brahmin.\""}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":48,"text":"यदि मां नाभिगच्छेथा युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः ।\nशपेयं त्वां महाराज पराभावाय सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you had not come to me, resolved to fight, great king, I would have cursed you for your total defeat.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"तद्युधिष्ठिर तुष्टोऽस्मि पूजितश्च त्वयानघ ।\nअनुजानामि युध्यस्व विजयं समवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, Yudhishthira, I am pleased and honored by you, sinless one. I give you leave. Fight and win.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"करवाणि च ते कामं ब्रूहि यत्तेऽभिकाङ्क्षितम् ।\nएवं गते महाराज युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will also fulfil your wish. Say what you desire. Since you have come thus, great king, what do you want other than my not fighting?\""}},{"n":51,"text":"अर्थस्य पुरुषो दासो दासस्त्वर्थो न कस्यचित् ।\nइति सत्यं महाराज बद्धोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man is the slave of wealth, but wealth is no one's slave. This is true, great king, and I am bound by wealth to the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"अतस्त्वां क्लीबवद्ब्रूमो युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ।\nयोत्स्यामि कौरवस्यार्थे तवाशास्यो जयो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So I speak like a eunuch: what do you want, other than my not fighting? I will fight for the Kaurava, but I shall wish you victory.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":53,"text":"जयमाशास्स्व मे ब्रह्मन्मन्त्रयस्व च मद्धितम् ।\nयुध्यस्व कौरवस्यार्थे वर एष वृतो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Wish me victory, brahmin, and counsel what is good for me. Fight for the Kaurava; this is the boon I choose.\""}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":54,"text":"ध्रुवस्ते विजयो राजन्यस्य मन्त्री हरिस्तव ।\nअहं च त्वाभिजानामि रणे शत्रून्विजेष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your victory is certain, king, since Hari is your counselor. I too know that you will conquer your enemies in battle.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"यतो धर्मस्ततः कृष्णो यतः कृष्णस्ततो जयः ।\nयुध्यस्व गच्छ कौन्तेय पृच्छ मां किं ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where there is dharma, there is Krishna; where Krishna is, there is victory. Go, son of Kunti, and fight. Ask me what else I may tell you.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":56,"text":"पृच्छामि त्वां द्विजश्रेष्ठ शृणु मे यद्विवक्षितम् ।\nकथं जयेयं संग्रामे भवन्तमपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask you, best of brahmins, hear what I wish to say: how can I defeat you, unconquered, in battle?\""}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":57,"text":"न तेऽस्ति विजयस्तावद्यावद्युध्याम्यहं रणे ।\nममाशु निधने राजन्यतस्व सह सोदरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is no victory for you so long as I fight in battle. Strive, with your brothers, for my swift death, king.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":58,"text":"हन्त तस्मान्महाबाहो वधोपायं वदात्मनः ।\nआचार्य प्रणिपत्यैष पृच्छामि त्वां नमोऽस्तु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, mighty-armed teacher, tell me the means of your own death. I bow to you and ask it, falling at your feet.\""}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":59,"text":"न शत्रुं तात पश्यामि यो मां हन्याद्रणे स्थितम् ।\nयुध्यमानं सुसंरब्धं शरवर्षौघवर्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear child, I see no enemy who could kill me while I stand in battle, fighting furiously and raining floods of arrows.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"ऋते प्रायगतं राजन्न्यस्तशस्त्रमचेतनम् ।\nहन्यान्मां युधि योधानां सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Except when I am unconscious, with weapons laid down and resolved to die, no warrior could kill me in battle. This I tell you truly.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"शस्त्रं चाहं रणे जह्यां श्रुत्वा सुमहदप्रियम् ।\nश्रद्धेयवाक्यात्पुरुषादेतत्सत्यं ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And I would throw down my weapon in battle on hearing some very painful news from a man whose word can be trusted. This I tell you truly.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":62,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा महाराज भारद्वाजस्य धीमतः ।\nअनुमान्य तमाचार्यं प्रायाच्छारद्वतं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from the wise son of Bharadvaja, great king, the Pandava honored that teacher and went to the son of Sharadvat, Kripa."}},{"n":63,"text":"सोऽभिवाद्य कृपं राजा कृत्वा चापि प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nउवाच दुर्धर्षतमं वाक्यं वाक्यविशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king greeted Kripa and circled him respectfully, then, skilled in speech, spoke words hard for others to bear."}},{"n":64,"text":"अनुमानये त्वां योत्स्यामि गुरो विगतकल्मषः ।\nजयेयं च रिपून्सर्वाननुज्ञातस्त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask your leave, teacher. I shall fight free of sin, and with your permission may I defeat all my enemies, sinless one.\""}},{"text":"कृप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kripa said:"}},{"n":65,"text":"यदि मां नाभिगच्छेथा युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः ।\nशपेयं त्वां महाराज पराभावाय सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you had not come to me, resolved to fight, great king, I would have cursed you for your total defeat.\""}},{"n":66,"text":"अर्थस्य पुरुषो दासो दासस्त्वर्थो न कस्यचित् ।\nइति सत्यं महाराज बद्धोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man is the slave of wealth, but wealth is no one's slave. This is true, great king, and I am bound by wealth to the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":67,"text":"तेषामर्थे महाराज योद्धव्यमिति मे मतिः ।\nअतस्त्वां क्लीबवद्ब्रूमि युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My view is that I must fight for them, great king. So I speak like a eunuch: what do you want, other than my not fighting?\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":68,"text":"हन्त पृच्छामि ते तस्मादाचार्य शृणु मे वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I ask you, teacher, hear my words.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":69,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा व्यथितो राजा नोवाच गतचेतनः ।\nतं गौतमः प्रत्युवाच विज्ञायास्य विवक्षितम् ।\nअवध्योऽहं महीपाल युध्यस्व जयमाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the king, troubled and bereft of his senses, could say no more. Gautama Kripa, understanding what he meant, replied: \"I cannot be killed, lord of the earth. Fight and win.\""}},{"n":70,"text":"प्रीतस्त्वभिगमेनाहं जयं तव नराधिप ।\nआशासिष्ये सदोत्थाय सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased by your coming, king. I shall rise each day and wish you victory. This I tell you truly.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा महाराज गौतमस्य वचस्तदा ।\nअनुमान्य कृपं राजा प्रययौ येन मद्रराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Gautama's words, great king, the king honored Kripa and went to where the king of Madra stood."}},{"n":72,"text":"स शल्यमभिवाद्याथ कृत्वा चाभिप्रदक्षिणम् ।\nउवाच राजा दुर्धर्षमात्मनिःश्रेयसं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having greeted Shalya and circled him respectfully, the king spoke to the invincible one words for his own highest good."}},{"n":73,"text":"अनुमानये त्वां योत्स्यामि गुरो विगतकल्मषः ।\nजयेयं च महाराज अनुज्ञातस्त्वया रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I ask your leave, teacher. I shall fight free of sin, and with your permission, great king, may I defeat my enemies.\""}},{"text":"शल्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shalya said:"}},{"n":74,"text":"यदि मां नाभिगच्छेथा युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः ।\nशपेयं त्वां महाराज पराभावाय वै रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you had not come to me, resolved to fight, great king, I would have cursed you for your defeat in battle.\""}},{"n":75,"text":"तुष्टोऽस्मि पूजितश्चास्मि यत्काङ्क्षसि तदस्तु ते ।\nअनुजानामि चैव त्वां युध्यस्व जयमाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am pleased and honored. May you have whatever you wish. I give you leave: fight and win.\""}},{"n":76,"text":"ब्रूहि चैव परं वीर केनार्थः किं ददामि ते ।\nएवं गते महाराज युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Say also, hero, what you need, and what I may give you. Since you have come thus, great king, what do you want other than my not fighting?\""}},{"n":77,"text":"अर्थस्य पुरुषो दासो दासस्त्वर्थो न कस्यचित् ।\nइति सत्यं महाराज बद्धोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man is the slave of wealth, but wealth is no one's slave. This is true, great king, and I am bound by wealth to the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":78,"text":"करिष्यामि हि ते कामं भागिनेय यथेप्सितम् ।\nब्रवीम्यतः क्लीबवत्त्वां युद्धादन्यत्किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will do what you wish, my sister's son, as you desire. So I speak like a eunuch: what do you want, other than my not fighting?\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":79,"text":"मन्त्रयस्व महाराज नित्यं मद्धितमुत्तमम् ।\nकामं युध्य परस्यार्थे वरमेतद्वृणोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great king, always give me your best counsel, and fight as you wish for the other side. This is the boon I choose.\""}},{"text":"शल्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shalya said:"}},{"n":80,"text":"ब्रूहि किमत्र साह्यं ते करोमि नृपसत्तम ।\nकामं योत्स्ये परस्यार्थे वृतोऽस्म्यर्थेन कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me, best of kings, what help can I give you here? I shall fight for the other side as I please, for I am bound by wealth to the Kauravas.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":81,"text":"स एव मे वरः सत्य उद्योगे यस्त्वया कृतः ।\nसूतपुत्रस्य संग्रामे कार्यस्तेजोवधस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The boon I ask is the one you truthfully promised during the preparations: in battle you must blunt the fire of the charioteer's son, Karna.\""}},{"text":"शल्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shalya said:"}},{"n":82,"text":"संपत्स्यत्येष ते कामः कुन्तीपुत्र यथेप्सितः ।\nगच्छ युध्यस्व विस्रब्धं प्रतिजाने जयं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This wish of yours will be fulfilled, son of Kunti, just as you desire. Go and fight without fear. I promise you victory.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":83,"text":"अनुमान्याथ कौन्तेयो मातुलं मद्रकेश्वरम् ।\nनिर्जगाम महासैन्याद्भ्रातृभिः परिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honored his maternal uncle, the lord of Madra, the son of Kunti left the great army, surrounded by his brothers."}},{"n":84,"text":"वासुदेवस्तु राधेयमाहवेऽभिजगाम वै ।\nतत एनमुवाचेदं पाण्डवार्थे गदाग्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva, elder brother of Gada, went to Radheya Karna in the battle, and for the Pandavas' sake spoke to him."}},{"n":85,"text":"श्रुतं मे कर्ण भीष्मस्य द्वेषात्किल न योत्स्यसि ।\nअस्मान्वरय राधेय यावद्भीष्मो न हन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have heard, Karna, that out of hatred for Bhishma you will not fight. Choose us, Radheya, until Bhishma is killed.\""}},{"n":86,"text":"हते तु भीष्मे राधेय पुनरेष्यसि संयुगे ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य साहाय्यं यदि पश्यसि चेत्समम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When Bhishma is slain, Radheya, you can return to the fight, if you think helping Dhritarashtra's son is the right course.\""}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":87,"text":"न विप्रियं करिष्यामि धार्तराष्ट्रस्य केशव ।\nत्यक्तप्राणं हि मां विद्धि दुर्योधनहितैषिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall not do anything displeasing to Dhritarashtra's son, Keshava. Know me as one who has given up his life for Duryodhana's good.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":88,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं कृष्णः संन्यवर्तत भारत ।\nयुधिष्ठिरपुरोगैश्च पाण्डवैः सह संगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that, Krishna turned back, O Bharata, and joined the Pandavas with Yudhishthira at their head."}},{"n":89,"text":"अथ सैन्यस्य मध्ये तु प्राक्रोशत्पाण्डवाग्रजः ।\nयोऽस्मान्वृणोति तदहं वरये साह्यकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the middle of the army, the eldest Pandava called out: \"Whoever chooses us, I will choose him as an ally.\""}},{"n":90,"text":"अथ तान्समभिप्रेक्ष्य युयुत्सुरिदमब्रवीत् ।\nप्रीतात्मा धर्मराजानं कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yuyutsu, looking at them, joyfully said to Yudhishthira, the righteous king, son of Kunti,"}},{"n":91,"text":"अहं योत्स्यामि मिषतः संयुगे धार्तराष्ट्रजान् ।\nयुष्मदर्थे महाराज यदि मां वृणुषेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will fight Dhritarashtra's sons in battle, before the eyes of all, for your sake, great king, if you will accept me, sinless one.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":92,"text":"एह्येहि सर्वे योत्स्यामस्तव भ्रातॄनपण्डितान् ।\nयुयुत्सो वासुदेवश्च वयं च ब्रूम सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come, come! We will all fight your foolish brothers. Yuyutsu, Vasudeva and we all say so.\""}},{"n":93,"text":"वृणोमि त्वां महाबाहो युध्यस्व मम कारणात् ।\nत्वयि पिण्डश्च तन्तुश्च धृतराष्ट्रस्य दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I choose you, mighty-armed one. Fight for me. In you the line and the offering of funeral cakes of Dhritarashtra will be seen to continue.\""}},{"n":94,"text":"भजस्वास्मान्राजपुत्र भजमानान्महाद्युते ।\nन भविष्यति दुर्बुद्धिर्धार्तराष्ट्रोऽत्यमर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Serve us, prince of great radiance, as we serve you. The wicked and very wrathful son of Dhritarashtra will not remain.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":95,"text":"ततो युयुत्सुः कौरव्यः परित्यज्य सुतांस्तव ।\nजगाम पाण्डुपुत्राणां सेनां विश्राव्य दुन्दुभिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yuyutsu, the Kaurava, left your sons and, proclaiming it with a drum, went over to the army of the sons of Pandu."}},{"n":96,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा संप्रहृष्टः सहानुजैः ।\nजग्राह कवचं भूयो दीप्तिमत्कनकोज्ज्वलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, greatly delighted with his younger brothers, put on his shining golden armor once more."}},{"n":97,"text":"प्रत्यपद्यन्त ते सर्वे रथान्स्वान्पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nततो व्यूहं यथापूर्वं प्रत्यव्यूहन्त ते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those bulls among men took to their own chariots, and again drew up their battle formation as before."}},{"n":98,"text":"अवादयन्दुन्दुभींश्च शतशश्चैव पुष्करान् ।\nसिंहनादांश्च विविधान्विनेदुः पुरुषर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They sounded drums and hundreds of tabors, and those bulls among men roared various lion-roars."}},{"n":99,"text":"रथस्थान्पुरुषव्याघ्रान्पाण्डवान्प्रेक्ष्य पार्थिवाः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नादयः सर्वे पुनर्जहृषिरे मुदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas, tigers among men, standing on their chariots, the kings led by Dhrishtadyumna rejoiced again with delight."}},{"n":100,"text":"गौरवं पाण्डुपुत्राणां मान्यान्मानयतां च तान् ।\nदृष्ट्वा महीक्षितस्तत्र पूजयां चक्रिरे भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing there the respect of the sons of Pandu, who honored those worthy of honor, the kings praised them greatly."}},{"n":101,"text":"सौहृदं च कृपां चैव प्राप्तकालं महात्मनाम् ।\nदयां च ज्ञातिषु परां कथयां चक्रिरे नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings spoke of the goodwill, kindness and timely conduct of those great souls, and of their deep compassion toward their kinsmen."}},{"n":102,"text":"साधु साध्विति सर्वत्र निश्चेरुः स्तुतिसंहिताः ।\nवाचः पुण्याः कीर्तिमतां मनोहृदयहर्षिणीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everywhere cries of \"Well done, well done!\" went up, full of praise, holy words of the renowned, delighting mind and heart."}},{"n":103,"text":"म्लेच्छाश्चार्याश्च ये तत्र ददृशुः शुश्रुवुस्तदा ।\nवृत्तं तत्पाण्डुपुत्राणां रुरुदुस्ते सगद्गदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the mlecchas and the Aryas who saw and heard of the conduct of the sons of Pandu wept with choking voices."}},{"n":104,"text":"ततो जघ्नुर्महाभेरीः शतशश्चैव पुष्करान् ।\nशङ्खांश्च गोक्षीरनिभान्दध्मुर्हृष्टा मनस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they struck the great drums, and hundreds of tabors, and the proud warriors joyfully blew conches white as cow's milk."}}]}]}